 "notes": "Widgets are only on pages 4-5 (the two application pages); pages 0-3 are instructions (no blanks, no widgets). Visible blanks with NO widgets that the applicant (or acceptance agent) fills: on page 4, the 'Identifying Documents' blocks (document type boxes, name, issue/exp. dates, ID no, state/country of issuance; completed at the acceptance facility), the applicant's legal signature line and two parent/guardian signature lines, and the staff/agent signature, date, agent/facility ID boxes, courier name, the 'For Issuing Office Only' line and the D/O/S/NFR, End. # and Exp. boxes at top right; on page 5 the 'For issuing office only' block, and the 'Other' write-in next to Additional # Other. None of these are GT (fillable GT = widgets). Same-name kid groups: 'Selection' (Book/Card/Both), 'Regular or Large Book', 'Gender' (M/F) and 'Additional #' (Home/Work/Cell/Other) are enum options, so equals for all kids; 'Ever Married', 'Spouse US Citizen', 'Divorced' and 'Ever Applied or Issued' are Yes/No kids under one name mapped to a boolean, so they have a path and no transforms (the op differs per kid). Parents map to parents[] (two blocks, one row each); their Sex and U.S. Citizen boxes are checkboxes inside repeated blocks, so pathless. 'List all other names you have used' A/B are list items (pathless)."
